This option uses CommunityToolkit.Mvvm 8.4.0; reference that package in
the project. A manual notifying implementation is also valid.

```csharp
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using CommunityToolkit.Mvvm.ComponentModel;
using CommunityToolkit.Mvvm.Input;

namespace MyApp.ViewModels;

public sealed partial class ProductDetailViewModel : ObservableObject
{
    private readonly IProductService _products;

    public ProductDetailViewModel(IProductService products) =>
        _products = products;

    [ObservableProperty]
    private string name = string.Empty;

    [ObservableProperty]
    private decimal price;

    [ObservableProperty]
    private bool isAvailable;

    [RelayCommand]
    private async Task LoadAsync()
    {
        var product = await _products.GetProductAsync();
        Name = product.Name;
        Price = product.Price;
        IsAvailable = product.IsAvailable;
    }
}

public interface IProductService
{
    Task<Product> GetProductAsync();
}

public sealed record Product(string Name, decimal Price, bool IsAvailable);
```

The generator exposes Name, Price and IsAvailable with setters that
raise PropertyChanged for those public names. LoadAsync generates the
asynchronous LoadCommand without an unrequested parameter. Bind to
those public members and assign the ViewModel as BindingContext.
